BT /F1 11 Tf 60 760 Td 15 TL
(Ant Colony Optimization: A Short Survey) '
() '
(Ants find short paths between nest and food without any central control. Each ant) '
(deposits pheromone as it walks. Shorter paths are completed faster, so they accumulate) '
(pheromone more quickly, which attracts more ants: a positive feedback loop. This) '
(indirect coordination through the environment is called stigmergy.) '
() '
(Pheromone evaporation is essential. Without it, the colony would lock in on the first) '
(path found, even a poor one. Evaporation acts as forgetting: trails that are not) '
(reinforced fade, letting the colony adapt when conditions change.) '
() '
ET
endstream
endobj
